Package: stackcallr
Title: Statically Inspect and Visualize the Call Tree of a Function
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Martin", "Frigaard", , "mjfrigaard@pm.me", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Builds the call tree of a function from its source code,
    without running it. Given a function name, the function's body is
    parsed to find every function it calls, and those calls are followed
    recursively, resolving 'UseMethod()' dispatch into the registered S3
    methods. The resulting tree is printed as an indented outline.
